## Setup — Spring Boot 3 + Micrometer Tracing

```xml
<!-- pom.xml -->
<dependency>
    <groupId>io.micrometer</groupId>
    <artifactId>micrometer-tracing-bridge-brave</artifactId>
</dependency>
<dependency>
    <groupId>io.zipkin.reporter2</groupId>
    <artifactId>zipkin-reporter-brave</artifactId>
</dependency>
<dependency>
    <groupId>io.github.openfeign</groupId>
    <artifactId>feign-micrometer</artifactId>  <!-- Feign auto-propagation -->
</dependency>
```

```yaml
# application.yml
management:
  tracing:
    sampling:
      probability: 0.1   # Trace 10% of requests in production
                         # Use 1.0 in development for full tracing
    propagation:
      type: W3C          # Industry standard: traceparent header
      # OR: B3 (older Zipkin format)

spring:
  zipkin:
    base-url: http://zipkin:9411  # Zipkin server URL
  sleuth:                         # Still works in older SB versions
    sampler:
      probability: 0.1

logging:
  pattern:
    level: "%5p [${spring.application.name},%X{traceId},%X{spanId}]"
    # Example log output:
    # INFO  [order-service,a1b2c3d4,e5f6a7b8] Order created
```

## How Trace Context Propagates

```
User → API Gateway → Order Service → Inventory Service → Database

HTTP Request from client:
  GET /api/orders/42
  (no trace headers yet)

Gateway generates trace:
  traceparent: 00-a1b2c3d4e5f6g7h8-f1e2d3c4-01
               ^^  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^  ^^^^^^^^  ^^
               ver  trace-id (16B)  span-id   flags

Gateway → Order Service:
  traceparent: 00-a1b2c3d4e5f6g7h8-f1e2d3c4-01  (same trace, new span)
  [Order Service creates span with parent = f1e2d3c4]

Order Service → Inventory Service:
  traceparent: 00-a1b2c3d4e5f6g7h8-a1b2c3d4-01  (same trace, new span)
  [Inventory Service creates span with parent = a1b2c3d4]

All spans reported to Zipkin → visualized as:
  ──────── Gateway (200ms) ──────────────────────
    ───── Order Service (150ms) ────────────────
      ── Inventory Service (80ms) ────────
      ── DB Query (30ms) ──────
```

## Logging with Trace ID (MDC)

```java
@Service
@Slf4j
public class OrderService {

    // Micrometer Tracing automatically adds traceId/spanId to MDC
    // So every log statement includes them automatically:
    public Order createOrder(CreateOrderRequest request) {
        log.info("Creating order for userId={}", request.getUserId());
        // Logs: INFO [order-service,a1b2c3d4,e5f6a7b8] Creating order for userId=42

        Order order = orderRepository.save(buildOrder(request));
        log.info("Order created orderId={}", order.getId());
        // Logs: INFO [order-service,a1b2c3d4,e5f6a7b8] Order created orderId=1001

        return order;
    }
}

// Manual span creation for custom operations:
@Service
public class PaymentService {

    private final Tracer tracer;  // Micrometer Tracer

    public PaymentResult processPayment(PaymentRequest request) {
        // Create custom span for a significant sub-operation:
        Span span = tracer.nextSpan().name("fraud-check").start();
        try (Tracer.SpanInScope ignored = tracer.withSpan(span)) {
            span.tag("paymentAmount", request.getAmount().toString());
            span.tag("currency", request.getCurrency());

            FraudCheckResult result = fraudService.check(request);

            span.tag("fraudScore", String.valueOf(result.getScore()));
            return processIfSafe(request, result);
        } catch (Exception e) {
            span.error(e);
            throw e;
        } finally {
            span.end();  // Always end the span!
        }
    }
}
```

## Zipkin vs Jaeger

```
Feature          | Zipkin                  | Jaeger
-----------------|-------------------------|---------------------------
Origin           | Twitter                 | Uber
Storage          | In-memory, MySQL, ES    | Cassandra, Elasticsearch
UI               | Simple timeline view    | Rich dependency graphs
Protocol         | Zipkin B3 / W3C         | Jaeger / OpenTelemetry
Spring support   | Native (brave reporter) | Via OpenTelemetry bridge
Recommendation   | Simple setups           | Production at scale

# Both integrate similarly with Spring Boot 3 + Micrometer
# Use OpenTelemetry SDK if you want vendor-neutral tracing
```

## Production Reality

Never trace 100% in production — a 1% sampling rate is often enough to understand p99 latencies and find bottlenecks. Only raise sampling for active debugging. The single biggest value-add: ensure trace ID is in every log line (MDC pattern). When a user reports issue at 2:47pm, you grep logs by trace ID and immediately have the full picture across services — no more "let me check service A... now service B... now correlate timestamps manually."
